1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,730
EMPLOYEE: Hello, Picturerep. Can I help you?

2
00:00:03,730 --> 00:00:08,384
WOMAN: Oh, hi. I saw your advertisement about copying pictures to disk

3
00:00:08,384 --> 00:00:12,650
and I'd like a bit more information about what you do.

4
00:00:12,650 --> 00:00:15,250
EMPLOYEE: Sure. What would you like to know?

5
00:00:15,250 --> 00:00:22,080
WOMAN: Well, I've got a box full of old family photos that's been up in the attic for years

6
00:00:22,540 --> 00:00:25,564
some of them must be 50 or 60 years old,

7
00:00:25,564 --> 00:00:29,120
and I'd like to get them converted to digital format.

8
00:00:29,120 --> 00:00:31,210
EMPLOYEE: Sure, we can do that for you.

9
00:00:31,210 --> 00:00:34,430
WOMAN: Right. And what about size?

10
00:00:34,430 --> 00:00:39,880
The photos are all sorts of sizes - are there any restrictions?

11
00:00:39,880 --> 00:00:46,330
EMPLOYEE: Well the maximum size of photo we can do with our normal service is 30 centimetres.

12
00:00:46,330 --> 00:00:49,780
And each picture must be at least 4 centimetres

13
00:00:49,940 --> 00:00:51,940
that's the minimum we can cope with.

14
00:00:51,940 --> 00:00:53,140
WOMAN: That should be fine.

15
00:00:53,140 --> 00:00:58,800
And some of them are in a frame - should I take them out before I send them?

16
00:00:58,800 --> 00:01:01,710
EMPLOYEE: Yes please, we can't copy them otherwise.

17
00:01:01,710 --> 00:01:06,640
And also the photos must all be separate, they mustn't be stuck into an album.

18
00:01:06,640 --> 00:01:09,100
WOMAN: OK, that's not a problem.

19
00:01:09,100 --> 00:01:13,490
So can you give me an idea of how much this will cost?

20
00:01:13,490 --> 00:01:17,850
I've got about 360 photos I think.

21
00:01:17,850 --> 00:01:24,880
EMPLOYEE: We charge £195 for 300 to 400 photos for the basic service.

22
00:01:24,880 --> 00:01:28,590
WOMAN: OK. And does that include the disk?

23
00:01:28,590 --> 00:01:33,410
EMPLOYEE: Yes, one disk - but you can get extra ones for £5 each.

24
00:01:33,410 --> 00:01:38,290
WOMAN: That's good. So do I need to pay when I send you the photos?

25
00:01:38,290 --> 00:01:42,690
EMPLOYEE: No, we won't need anything until we've actually copied the pictures.

26
00:01:42,690 --> 00:01:45,620
Then we'll let you know how much it is

27
00:01:45,620 --> 00:01:49,560
and once we've received the payment, we'll send the parcel off to you.

28
00:01:49,560 --> 00:01:53,710
WOMAN: Right.

29
00:01:53,710 --> 00:01:57,500
EMPLOYEE: Is there anything else you'd like to ask about our services?

30
00:01:57,500 --> 00:02:01,467
WOMAN: Yes. I've roughly sorted out the photos into groups,

31
00:02:01,467 --> 00:02:04,420
according to what they're about

32
00:02:04,960 --> 00:02:08,210
so can you keep them in those groups when you copy them.

33
00:02:08,210 --> 00:02:13,623
EMPLOYEE: Sure. We'll save each group in a different folder on the disk and if you like,

34
00:02:13,623 --> 00:02:16,170
you can suggest a name for each folder.

35
00:02:16,170 --> 00:02:20,650
WOMAN: So I could have one called 'Grandparents' for instance?

36
00:02:20,650 --> 00:02:22,130
EMPLOYEE: Exactly.

37
00:02:22,130 --> 00:02:26,320
WOMAN: And do you do anything besides scan the photos

38
00:02:27,080 --> 00:02:29,340
Like, can you make any improvements?

39
00:02:29,340 --> 00:02:33,067
EMPLOYEE: Yes, in the standard service each photo is checked,

40
00:02:33,067 --> 00:02:36,860
and we can sometimes touch up the colour a bit

41
00:02:36,880 --> 00:02:40,520
or improve the contrast - that can make a big difference.

42
00:02:40,520 --> 00:02:44,716
WOMAN: OK. And some of the photos are actually quite fragile -

43
00:02:44,716 --> 00:02:48,150
they won't get damaged in the process, will they?

44
00:02:48,150 --> 00:02:52,890
EMPLOYEE: No, if any look particularly fragile, we'd do them by hand.

45
00:02:52,890 --> 00:02:56,230
We do realise how precious these old photos can be.

46
00:02:56,230 --> 00:02:57,270
WOMAN: Sure.

47
00:02:57,270 --> 00:03:02,374
EMPLOYEE: And another thing is we can make changes to a photo if you want -

48
00:03:02,374 --> 00:03:05,440
so if you want to remove an object from a photo

49
00:03:05,700 --> 00:03:09,180
or maybe alter the background, we can do that.

50
00:03:09,180 --> 00:03:12,480
WOMAN: Really? I might be interested in that.

51
00:03:12,480 --> 00:03:15,500
I'll have a look through the photos and see.

52
00:03:15,500 --> 00:03:22,210
Oh, and talking of fixing photos - I've got a few that aren't properly in focus.

53
00:03:22,210 --> 00:03:24,720
Can you do anything to make that better?

54
00:03:24,720 --> 00:03:28,440
EMPLOYEE: No, I'm afraid that's one thing we can't do.

55
00:03:28,440 --> 00:03:29,690
WOMAN: OK.

56
00:03:29,690 --> 00:03:31,990
EMPLOYEE: Any other information I can give you?

57
00:03:31,990 --> 00:03:36,160
WOMAN: Er... oh, how long will it all take?

58
00:03:36,160 --> 00:03:39,220
EMPLOYEE: We aim to get the copying done in ten days.

59
00:03:39,220 --> 00:03:44,420
WOMAN: Fine. Right, well I'll get the photos packed up in a box

60
00:03:44,420 --> 00:03:45,840
and post them off to you.

61
00:03:45,840 --> 00:03:50,188
EMPLOYEE: Right. If you've got a strong cardboard box, that's best.

62
00:03:50,188 --> 00:03:54,140
We've found that plastic ones sometimes break in the post.

63
00:03:54,140 --> 00:03:59,040
WOMAN: OK. Right, thanks for your help. Bye.

64
00:03:59,040 --> 00:04:01,000
EMPLOYEE: Bye.
